but it’s a bare static field with no initializer. Other optional subsystems 
(like Net) are explicitly annotated @Nullable, so the minimal, non-invasive fix 
is to mark gl30 as @Nullable as well, indicating it may be absent when GL30 is 
not available. This avoids forcing a dummy implementation and should not break 
existing code that already checks GL30 availability. I’ll update only that field
declaration, then run the targeted Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error 
count drops by exactly one and no new errors appear.

